Games/Doom is a game built on Snowstorm Engine, not part of the engine. It is
NOT covered by the repository's public-domain dedication (UNLICENSE.txt); this
file governs it instead.


WHY THIS DIRECTORY IS SEPARATE

Doom's interpreter is doomgeneric, and its music path uses Chocolate Doom's OPL
synthesiser, callback queue and MIDI sequencer. Both projects are GPL-2.0.

Neither is committed to this repository. The build fetches them at configure
time (Vendor/doomgeneric/CMakeLists.txt), and the default engine build
(SS_ENABLE_DOOM=OFF) neither fetches nor links them.

The code in this directory is original, but three of its files include those
projects' headers and implement interfaces they declare:

  Source/DoomSound.cpp   fills sound_module_t   (doomgeneric, i_sound.h)
  Source/DoomSystem.cpp  implements the DG_*    platform callbacks (doomgeneric.h)
  Source/OplDriver.c     implements the OPL_*   entry points (Chocolate Doom, opl.h)

Whether that makes those files derivative works of GPL code is genuinely
unsettled, and this project asserts nothing either way. The carve-out exists so
that the answer does not matter.


TERMS

